{"kind":"request","text":"codex: make chess playable for a first-time user — hugh usability review of the landed a1f130fa app, delivered in session and restated here whole; this request carries no rests_on because the merge successors went ordinarily stale in the post-merge accounting and nothing fresher exists, so the evidence stands self-contained. HEADLINE: not yet playable, because the instructions are not clear on how the second player joins. README, rewrite the first section for the user encountering all of this for the first time, and check the rest in the same voice: it never says how to create a key file (for example bob.key); it never says what create-record means; if games have names, the example should give the game a name — and if they do not, decide whether they should. UI, first-run experience: replace the how-it-works paragraph (\"Every position comes from the signed log. The server replays the same fold used by the command line. This view cannot sign or submit moves.\") with brief usage instructions in a popup help overlay, and for an open game the overlay must say how to tell your agent to join over MCP — that is the primary use case. UI, chrome: remove the \"Verified frontier \u003cid\u003e\" line; add a small GitHub link icon in the toolbar; retitle using hugh coinage — \"durable games: chess\" in the title rather than \"durable games\" on the lobby page; the lobby should say Lobby with the same breadcrumb style as the game page. UI, layout: header bar; header area with game info and players; board below on the left, chat on the right, chat panel resizable. UI, board: squares are not square (occupied cells render taller than unoccupied — fix the cell sizing); square tooltips should give the UCI coordinate. COPY: drop \"The process-local live room restarted. Its transient history was cleared\" entirely; \"No messages in this process-local room.\" becomes \"No chat messages yet.\"; \"The fold allows no move from that square.\" becomes \"No valid move is available from \u003csquare\u003e\" — fold is not user-visible vocabulary, and say why when the engine can tell (empty square, opponent piece, pinned, not your turn). Deliver as one lane: new head on a request branch from chess main a1f130fa, gates green including -race, exact-head artifacts, independent review by me, then hugh tries it again — playability by a fresh user is the acceptance test.","body":{"branch":"request/chess-first-user","conditions":"A first-time user can, from the README alone, create keys for two players, create a named game, join as the second player, and play; the help overlay teaches usage and the MCP join instruction for open games; frontier line removed, GitHub icon added, durable-games title, Lobby breadcrumb; header/board-left/chat-right layout with resizable chat; square cells rendered square with UCI-coordinate tooltips; the three copy changes exactly as specified with reason-bearing invalid-move messages where the engine knows the reason; gates green at the exact head including -race; exact-head artifacts and independent planner review; hugh accepts on a fresh-user walkthrough.","severity":"high","to":"09c97907402e7747d051c0c599d9eb463c48d19825820a3e4c433cde2e60e2a8"}}